BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wanted
DTSTART:20261018T170000Z
DTEND:20261018T191500Z
DTSTAMP:20261018T055910Z
UID:1007375
DESCRIPTION:<p>How far would you go to get everything you ever WANTED?<br 
 /><br />Texas\, 1893 &mdash\; Twin sisters Mary and Martha Clarke are on t
 he run. As Black women who pass for white and hide in plain sight\, they s
 traddle a dangerous line between two Americas. When powerful forces close 
 in to keep their family from claiming a future of their own\, Mary and Mar
 tha are driven to desperate measures to save their mother and their family
 &rsquo\;s legacy. Forced to do the unthinkable in order to survive\, the s
 isters fight for self-determination\, dignity\, and an inheritance long de
 nied. Through it all\, the Kinfolk\, a vibrant chorus of ancestors\, guide
  Mary and Martha forward on an odyssey of sisterhood\, rebellion\, and fre
 edom.<br /><br />A soulful and dangerous new Broadway musical inspired by 
 a Clarke family story carried for generations\, <em>Wanted</em> is the epi
 c tale of Mary and Martha: sisters\, outlaws\, legends. This <em>New York 
 Times</em> Critic&rsquo\;s Pick has been hailed as &ldquo\;thrillingly ori
 ginal&rdquo\; with an &ldquo\;audacious and rollicking story.&rdquo\; The 
 production stars Grammy&reg\; winner Ledisi as Tallulah Clarke\, Grammy no
 minee Luke James as Elijah\, Bradley Jaden as Jesse\, and Solea Pfeiffer a
 nd Liisi LaFontaine as Mary and Martha Clarke.<br /><br /><em>Wanted</em> 
 features book and lyrics by <em>Variety</em> &ldquo\;Star to Watch&rdquo\;
  Angelica Ch&eacute\;ri\, a descendant of the Sisters Clarke\, and music b
 y Richard Rodgers Award&ndash\;winning composer Ross Baum. The production 
 is directed by Tony Award nominee and Obie Award&reg\; winner Stevie Walke
 r-Webb\, with choreography by Chelsey Arce.</p>
LOCATION:James Earl Jones Theatre\, 138 West 48th Street\, New York NY 100
 36
END:VEVENT
